//! Empirical Adversarial Verification Suite — Challenger 2 (Milestone 5: Ticket T8)
//!
//! Focus: Cross-Language Integration & Cryptographic Parity:
//! 1. Bidirectional HMAC-SHA256 signature parity across Rust (`crypto::sign_payload`) and Python (`backend/app.py`):
//!    - Signatures generated by Rust are 100% accepted by Python Flask verification middleware.
//!    - Signatures generated by Python test helper are 100% accepted by Rust `crypto::verify_payload_signature`.
//! 2. Edge-case and boundary verification:
//!    - Exactly 30s timestamp skew boundary accepted by both.
//!    - 31s timestamp skew in past or future rejected by both with replay expiration.
//!    - Single-bit payload tampering rejected by both.
//!    - Secret key mismatch rejected by both.
//!    - Case-insensitive hex matching accepted by both.
//! 3. Live HTTP Interoperability:
//!    - Live Flask backend spawned on ephemeral localhost port.
//!    - Health check `/healthz` accessible without authentication.
//!    - Direct requests bypassing sidecar headers rejected with HTTP 401.
//!    - Direct requests signed by Rust client accepted with HTTP 200.
//!    - Full Axum Route B tool interception forwarding to live Flask over TCP with HMAC headers.
//!    - Policy enforcement choke-points (e.g. `/db/drop`, unauthorized role, invalid JWT) blocked at sidecar.

